* =====================================================================================================
* motor_drive__nrf52840_gpio.lib -- nRF52840 GPIO pad (standard drive) as seen by the motor-drive nets
*
* Part      : nRF52840 inside the Raytac MDBT50Q-U1MV2 module (main board U10)
* Datasheet : nRF52840 Product Specification v1.6+, section 6.9.3.1 GPIO electrical specification
*             (https://docs.nordicsemi.com/bundle/ps_nrf52840/page/gpio.html; values confirmed via
*             Nordic DevZone thread 48727 and 111050)
*
* Modelled (value, datasheet reference):
*   - Output, standard drive (S0S1): VOH,SD >= VDD - 0.4 V at 0.5 mA, VOL,SD <= 0.4 V at 0.5 mA,
*     represented as an ideal VDD/0 source behind rout = 0.4 V / 0.5 mA = 800 Ohm (the guaranteed
*     worst case; Nordic notes the real drop is far smaller).
*   - Pad capacitance cpad = 3 pF (assumed, the PS table value is not verified here).
*   - Input thresholds VIH = 0.7*VDD min, VIL = 0.3*VDD max: applied in the test code, not in SPICE.
*   - Optional internal pull resistor rpull (13 kOhm typ in the PS; param, default open = 1 GOhm)
*     to VDD (pullup=1) or to GND (pullup=0).
*
* NOT modelled: high-drive mode, slew-rate control, input leakage (sub-uA, negligible against the
*   100 kOhm and 33 kOhm loads here), ESD diodes beyond the abs-max rails.
* =====================================================================================================

.subckt NRF_GPIO_OUT PAD VDD GND CTRL params: rout=800 cpad=3p
* CTRL is a 0..1 V logic command
B1 x GND V = V(VDD,GND)*min(1, max(0, V(CTRL,GND)))
R1 x PAD {rout}
C1 PAD GND {cpad}
.ends NRF_GPIO_OUT

.subckt NRF_GPIO_IN PAD VDD GND params: cpad=3p rpull=1G pullup=1
C1 PAD GND {cpad}
R1 PAD pr {rpull}
B1 pr GND V = {pullup}*V(VDD,GND)
.ends NRF_GPIO_IN
